# Global gitignore -- symlinked to ~/.config/git/ignore by bin/setup.sh.
#
# git reads this path by default (XDG), so no core.excludesfile is needed.
# The old .gitignore.global in this repo was never wired up and therefore
# never did anything, so nothing was carried over from it.
#
# settings.local.json is per-machine permission and trust state that Claude Code
# rewrites on its own. Ignoring it here rather than per repository is deliberate:
# it is never committable anywhere, and a global rule cannot be forgotten in a
# new project.

.DS_Store
**/.claude/settings.local.json

# The goal ledgers the loop-goal skill keeps, at .loop/<slug>.md in whatever
# repository a loop is running in. Ignored globally for the same reason as the
# line above: a loop is started in any project, and a per-repository rule is one
# that gets forgotten in the next one. A ledger worth keeping is moved out of
# .loop/ and committed deliberately.
.loop/
